 abuse and  that I've received  um  it was it was quite a serious one right  you know with threats to my family it  was quite a serious one okay quite a  serious one sorry I'm sorry I mean you  know Dan Abbott faces this you know  David Lammy faces did  um quasi as you just mentioned faces  Kami faces this you know Rishi now is  facing it you know it's it's  unfortunately there are some people in  Britain who do not like to see people  with this different skin color uh in  positions of influence and power Boris  Johnson has written the past I know it  was a long time ago but he did talk  about out picking the knees and  watermelon Smiles did that trouble you I  think he might have apologized for those  um if you were to ask him again if he  will use those same language in another  book I'm sure he probably wouldn't see  that but personally  I don't there's any space there's any  room for that kind of language it's not  something I would well well let's get  back to you let's stop talking about all  these other politicians  you are as I said the fast black police  and crime session you yourself have been  stopped and searched I think at least  six times yes is that correct yeah yeah  three times in London uh when I was  growing up here once in Hertfordshire  once in buckinghamshire and once in  bedfordshire I wanted to ask you like  has it happened to your sons do you  worry for your sons  thankfully hasn't happened to know my  children yet but the thing is this I  have used because I I train to be a  special Constable with benefits of  police before I became a police and  crime commissioner and I got to see for  myself firsthand how the powers are used  I saw this I got to see the necessity of  it and it's something that we need that  the police need to have in their Arsenal  in keeping our communities safe  but it's not it is a blunt tool so you  support it I support the appropriate use  of it right uh and the justifiable so  it's used inappropriately often  sometimes with that question of course  okay wasn't I wasn't I think 19 years  old yeah I was coming from basketball  practice in White Chapel and my goal  stopped and I asked the officer why did  you stop me and he said to me just to  make sure you know one of London's Most  Wanted  that was it  how'd you thought maybe were you angry  at the time I didn't really care because  I need a lot of my friends dealt with  that but the older I got knowing what I  know now I'm like well that's kind of  that was just wrong there was no need  for that I just would love to see  policing also understand how its  coercive Powers have an impact on people  um who are most affected by it I mean  someone called you a traitor when you  took this job was that  was it painful for you but did you  understand why can you understand no I  can understand why absolutely not I mean  you know I I I'm a conservative because  I want to be I know my history as a  black person I know the history of this  country I'm not in denial of it I  welcome and celebrate the good but you  know I of course I will have to accept  they're not very good as well uh but the  conservative party is not  um a um a monolithic group for someone  to give me grief just because I'm in one  political party and dating the color of  my skin should not fit into that  political part I think it's just oh was  it because because people feel that the  police is institutionally racist and  it's disproportionately targeting young  black men in stop and search Etc so  people are mistrustful well I mean I've  been call Trader for that as well you  know you know but you know my thing is  this  um I feel very passionate about Law and  Order  um but there are those who like Carrick  who really are total shame to the  uniform that they wear but I'm here  because I want to make policing better  for all of our communities in London  where you grew up black londoners make  up 13 of the capital's total population  yet account for 45 of London's kn